# `devkit schema` emits LF, and `tests/config_schema.rs` compares its output to
# this file byte for byte. Without this, Git for Windows checks it out as CRLF
# and the drift test fails over line endings Git itself introduced. The file
# also ships as a GitHub Release asset, where LF is what consumers expect.
schema/devkit-config.json text eol=lf

# Recorded goldens are compared byte for byte against freshly rendered output,
# which always uses LF. A CRLF checkout fails that comparison on line endings
# Git itself introduced.
crates/devkit-docs/tests/goldens/** text eol=lf
